# Story: As a truck driver, I want to move my booking to another slot, so that I can keep my container booked when I am running late. Rescheduling moves the booking to the new slot if it has room, frees the place in the old slot, and keeps the same booking reference. Moving to a full slot is refused with SLOT_FULL; moving to the same slot is refused with SAME_SLOT.

@draft
Feature: Rescheduling a Booking

  Scenario Outline: Moving a booking to another available slot
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for a valid container
    Then the booking is confirmed with a reference
    When I reschedule my booking to "<new_slot>"
    Then the outcome is "CONFIRMED"

    Examples:
      | new_slot             |
      | a gate slot tomorrow at 10:30 with room for 2 trucks |
      | a gate slot starting in 60 minutes with room for 1 truck |

  Scenario Outline: Moving to an already full slot
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for a valid container
    Then the booking is confirmed with a reference
    When I reschedule my booking to "<new_slot>"
    Then the outcome is refused because "SLOT_FULL"

    Examples:
      | new_slot             |
      | a gate slot tomorrow at 10:00 with room for 2 trucks |

  Scenario Outline: Moving to the same slot
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for a valid container
    Then the booking is confirmed with a reference
    When I reschedule my booking to "<new_slot>"
    Then the outcome is refused because "SAME_SLOT"

    Examples:
      | new_slot             |
      | a gate slot tomorrow at 10:30 with room for 2 trucks |

  Scenario Outline: Moving after change cutoff time
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for a valid container
